<title>JAPAN: Japan July pork imports drop 30.2 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan July pork imports drop 30.2 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's pork imports in July totalled 40,775 tonnes, down 30.2 percent from 58,417 tonnes in July 1995, Finance Ministry data released on Wednesday showed.</p>
<p>Details were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    July 96	June 96	July 95</p>
<p> Total	     40,775	145,523	 58,417</p>
<p> Refrigerated    15,604	 16,312	 15,153</p>
<p> Frozen	    25,171	129,211	 43,264</p>
<p>Major suppliers of refrigerated pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p> Taiwan	     7,585	  8,374	  8,318</p>
<p> U.S.		 6,864	  6,831	  6,208</p>
<p>Major supplier of frozen pork (in tonnes):</p>
<p>		    July 96	June 96	July 95</p>
<p> Taiwan	    10,681	 37,350	 15,653</p>
<p>Imports of refrigerated pork in the first seven months of calendar 1996 totalled 100,680 tonnes, against 90,575 tonnes in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>Imports of frozen pork in the first seven months of calendar 1996 came to 479,798 tonnes, against 222,319 tonnes in the same period of 1995, ministry data showed.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk</p>
</text>
